"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[4128],{74128:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"schemaVersion":1,"locale":"en","slug":"01-dohod-i-bogatstvo","title":"Lesson 01. Income and wealth: What your work is worth and how long you can live without pay","sourceFingerprint":"cd16fc00fc353f396da0753d8b5f1297044bb666b560889b580bd70f8346b33d","blocks":[{"id":"b001","markdown":"## Income and wealth"},{"id":"b002","markdown":"What your work is worth and how long you can live without pay"},{"id":"b003","markdown":"Before deciding how to spend and save, answer 2 questions: where money really comes from and what counts as wealth. Most people answer both incorrectly and spend years running in the wrong direction."},{"id":"b004","markdown":"### Salary is a price"},{"id":"b005","markdown":"“Money comes from work” describes a channel. The reason goes deeper: you are paid for solving someone’s problem. How much depends on the value of that problem and how hard you are to replace."},{"id":"b006","markdown":"An employer does not pay for fatigue, years of study or office hours. It buys a result like any other product. A product’s price depends on 2 things: how much money it makes or saves its buyer, and how many alternatives are available."},{"id":"b007","markdown":"An example from my profession. A company employs 2 designers, both working 40 hours a week. One makes social-media banners. The other redesigns a bank app’s payment screen, through which millions of rubles pass daily. If those changes make just 1% more users finish payment, the bank earns enough to cover that designer’s salary comfortably."},{"id":"b008","markdown":"Both get tired and do necessary work. But thousands of people can make banners. Very few understand how a screen affects the bank’s money. Fairness is not the issue: scarce skills and the money passing through your work create the salary difference."},{"id":"b009","markdown":"### 4 levers"},{"id":"b010","markdown":"I have built digital products for over 10 years. When a product cannot command a higher price, a team usually has 4 levers. You have the same ones."},{"id":"b011","markdown":"Solve a more expensive problem. An accountant at a beauty salon and one at a bank do similar work. But an error at the bank costs thousands of times more, so accuracy commands higher pay. Where does the most money pass through your profession, and can you move closer to it?"},{"id":"b012","markdown":"Become harder to replace. A skill everyone has is worth little. What commands a premium is 2 ordinary skills rarely found together: a lawyer who understands IT, a designer who understands finance, or an engineer who can sell."},{"id":"b013","markdown":"Sell more than hours. Hourly pay limits income to the hours available in a day. A course, template, service or your own team does not have that ceiling. You do not need to start a business tomorrow; simply remember the limit."},{"id":"b014","markdown":"Negotiate the price. This is the most underestimated lever. Companies generally raise pay just enough to keep someone from leaving. If you never show you could leave, there is little reason to increase it. Once a year, check vacancies and salary ranges in your profession so you at least know your market price."},{"id":"b015","markdown":"Extra jobs also increase income and can be necessary, for example to repay expensive debt quickly. But there you sell more hours at the same price. Increasing the value of the hour itself can keep income higher permanently."},{"id":"b016","markdown":"### The price of your hour"},{"id":"b017","markdown":"Divide take-home pay by working hours per month, around 168 on average. From average accrued pay of 109 524 RUB (Rosstat, July 2026), about 95 300 RUB remains after 13% personal income tax. Divide by 168 hours: roughly 570 RUB per hour, and less if commuting time is included."},{"id":"b018","markdown":"Now translate any purchase into hours. A 1 700 RUB delivery dinner is 3 working hours; a 90 000 RUB phone is almost 4 working weeks; an unused 400 RUB monthly subscription consumes 8 hours a year. Nobody is telling you to reject everything. Every purchase simply has a visible real price. You will need this figure next lesson."},{"id":"b019","markdown":"How much is your hour worth, and how many hours does a purchase cost?"},{"id":"b020","markdown":"Take-home pay 95 300 RUB: 567 RUB per hour."},{"id":"b021","markdown":"Take-home pay \xf7 168 working hours."},{"id":"b022","markdown":"Delivery dinner \xb7 1 700 RUB: 3.0 hours. Phone \xb7 90 000 RUB: 159 hours. Subscription at 400 RUB a month, annually \xb7 4 800 RUB: 8.5 hours. You need not reject everything. Every purchase now has a visible real price."},{"id":"b023","markdown":"### Who counts as wealthy"},{"id":"b024","markdown":"Every car has a range: how many kilometres it can travel on the fuel in its tank. A huge SUV with a 400-horsepower engine looks more impressive than a small car. But imagine every petrol station on the route closes. The car with a full tank and modest consumption travels further, not the one with the most powerful engine."},{"id":"b025","markdown":"Money works the same way. Wealth is measured by how long you can live without earning. A large salary with a mortgage, car loan and empty account at month-end is a powerful engine with an empty tank. A modest salary with something saved each month eventually produces a long runway."},{"id":"b026","markdown":"Your runway is simple to calculate: savings divided by monthly expenses gives the number of months."},{"id":"b027","markdown":"- 0 months: living payday to payday; any breakdown or illness becomes debt."},{"id":"b028","markdown":"- 1–3 months: enough for a small setback, but not job loss."},{"id":"b029","markdown":"- 3–6 months: enough to search for another job."},{"id":"b030","markdown":"- 12 months or more: you can afford to choose."},{"id":"b031","markdown":"The next level, when capital income covers all expenses, is called financial independence. It is a car that refuels while moving."},{"id":"b032","markdown":"Most people are currently far from even the first step. In a Russian Field survey from late May and early June 2026, 60% of Russians had no savings. Among those with savings, the median runway was around 3.5 months. NIFI at the Finance Ministry and NAFI put the share without savings at around 24%. Methods differ, but the picture is similar: many have no reserve at all, and many others have only a few months."},{"id":"b033","markdown":"WHO GOES FURTHER? E F: 400-HORSEPOWER ENGINE, EMPTY TANK; HIGH SALARY, EMPTY ACCOUNT. E F: MODEST ENGINE, FULL TANK; SAVES SOMETHING EVERY MONTH. WEALTH = RUNWAY. How many months can you live without pay?"},{"id":"b034","markdown":"Money withdrawable within a week: 0 RUB. Monthly expenses: 70 000 RUB. Runway: 0.0 months."},{"id":"b035","markdown":"Runway: savings \xf7 expenses."},{"id":"b036","markdown":"You live payday to payday: any breakdown or illness becomes debt."},{"id":"b037","markdown":"### Why runway does not grow with pay"},{"id":"b038","markdown":"Have you noticed how cupboards work? Move to an apartment with twice the storage and, a year later, the new cupboards are as full as the old ones. Possessions expand to fill the space available."},{"id":"b039","markdown":"Money follows the same pattern. A raise pays for a better apartment, the next for a pricier car, and another for a more distant holiday. Each choice seems reasonable, but the gap between income and expenses does not grow; only living standards do. Psychologists call this hedonic adaptation: after a few months the novelty stops bringing pleasure, while the payments continue."},{"id":"b040","markdown":"Another approach works: immediately save a predetermined share of income and live on the rest calmly, without guilt. You can start with just 3%, aiming for 10–20% later. Lesson 3 explains choosing the share and making saving automatic."},{"id":"b041","markdown":"### Savings that cost more"},{"id":"b042","markdown":"The opposite mistake is cutting everything, including things that actually protect your money."},{"id":"b043","markdown":"Anyone who works at a computer knows this example. A slow work laptop wastes at least half an hour daily. That exceeds 120 working hours a year. At the hourly value above, around 570 RUB at average pay, it means about 70 000 RUB of lost time. That is almost the price of a decent new laptop, in just one year."},{"id":"b044","markdown":"Saving 30 000 RUB on winter tyres and driving another season on worn ones seems reasonable until the first accident, insurance excess and bodywork repair. Put off dentistry for a year and you may need root treatment rather than a filling. Buy the cheapest refrigerator and it can consume the price difference in electricity within a couple of years."},{"id":"b045","markdown":"Cut wasteful leaks, which the next lesson covers. It is better to protect spending that preserves health, time or money."},{"id":"b046","markdown":"Work income depends on health, the labour market and age. In 20–30 years you may not want the same pace. Savings do not become ill or old, and placed appropriately they can earn income themselves. The long-term task is gradually shifting the burden from yourself to capital: extending your runway."},{"id":"b047","markdown":"### Calculate 2 figures"},{"id":"b048","markdown":"- Your hourly price: take-home pay divided by 168."},{"id":"b049","markdown":"- Your runway: money withdrawable within a week without loss, such as deposits, savings accounts and cash, divided by monthly expenses. If expenses are unclear, use an estimate; next lesson we calculate them precisely."},{"id":"b050","markdown":"If runway is under a month, you are in the majority. This entire module is about moving that number."},{"id":"b051","markdown":"### The essentials"},{"id":"b052","markdown":"- Income is the price of a solved problem. Raise it in 4 ways: solve more expensive problems, become harder to replace, sell more than hours, and negotiate the price."},{"id":"b053","markdown":"- Wealth is measured by runway: how many months you can live without pay."},{"id":"b054","markdown":"- Spending grows with income as possessions fill any cupboard. The defence is saving a share immediately."},{"id":"b055","markdown":"- Cut leaks, not spending that protects health, time or money."},{"id":"b056","markdown":"Next lesson we discover where the money actually goes. It is usually an uncomfortable discovery."}],"terms":[{"id":"ndfl","term":"Personal income tax (NDFL)","definition":"Personal income tax. This course’s educational calculations use 13% up to 2.4 million RUB of annual income and 15% for the next band. Since 2025 the main scale has been progressive; special rules apply to other types of income. Check current rates and deduction eligibility with the Federal Tax Service."}],"quizzes":[{"id":"01-dohod-i-bogatstvo-q1","q":"Why can two people working the same number of hours earn very different amounts?","options":["Their work involves different amounts of money and they are differently hard to replace","One simply got lucky with a manager","Salary always depends only on education"],"correct":0},{"id":"01-dohod-i-bogatstvo-q2","q":"How do you calculate your financial runway in months?","options":["Add up every available credit limit","Divide salary by working days","Divide accessible savings by monthly expenses"],"correct":2},{"id":"01-dohod-i-bogatstvo-q3","q":"Take-home pay is 60 000 RUB with 168 working hours a month. How many working hours does a 3 600 RUB purchase cost?","options":["About 1 hour","About 10 hours","About 3.6 hours"],"correct":1}],"officialSources":[]}')}}]);